      "side": 1,
      "message": "`kvm_arch_destroy_vm()` will reclaim all the donated memory and by the end of this function, the PSCI counter (provided only 1 VM has ran) will be back to 0.\n\nNow, when crosvm is killed and the fd\u0027s for vCPUS, VM and KVM-devices are released, the only thing that can keep the VM alive are the stage-2 ptdump and access to the kvm stats. As none of that is expected to happen on a production system, I suppose this is safe to say after crosvm died, the VM has been teardown properly.",
